,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":12711.515023375,"data":"Limits\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":12711.515026997,"data":"- Same 95 missions and 5 recording days as E18b (one day, 2021-12-22, has only 10 missions): the seeds test training randomness, not new data.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":12711.515031076,"data":"- Scattering frequencies are normalised (cycles/sample), not Hz; the audio sample rate is unverified.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":12711.515035018,"data":"- The D arms differ in capacity from R1 (parameter counts above); they are therefore also judged against their own shuffled-audio controls (condition 7).\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":12711.515039027,"data":"- Only one attention layer per path and one strong/weak split rule (top half by fit-window energy) were tried; nothing was tuned on any fold.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":12711.515043069,"data":"- mamba-ssm CUDA kernels are not bit-deterministic; B0/R1 vs E18b is only a soft check.\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":12711.515046879,"data":"- The +0.01 threshold for condition 1 was chosen before the run because the audio-specific ceiling of R1 is about +0.02; each contrast is also reported against +0.02.\n"}
